EN = [
 {"t": "Header and ending", "items": [
  "Header: G21 G40 G90 G94 and on the next line G54. No G17, G49 or G80.",
  "Ending: G0 Z100. / M9 / G53 H0 Z0 / M30. No M5, G49 or G91 G28 (M30 already stops the spindle).",
  "If G52 was used, cancel it before the ending with G52 X0 Y0.",
  "T.. and M6 always on separate lines (on the Romi D1250 V6 it alarms if they are together).",
  "Every block ends with ; (macros and parametric), and the comment comes before the ; : #1 = 35 (HOLE DIAMETER) ;"]},
 {"t": "Macros (G65)", "items": [
  "Subprograms numbered from O1611 up (O16xx). Main programs O00xx.",
  "Sub header on the same line as the number: O1625 (COMMENT) ; and never a ; before the comment.",
  "Every comment in parentheses followed by ; (no parentheses inside the comment).",
  "Clean main program: only the header comment. The letter explanation and a call example go only in the sub, in the (G65 Pxxxx LETTERS) block.",
  "Standard main: % / O00xx (COMMENT) ; / G21 G40 G90 G94 ; / G54 ; / T10 ; / M6 ; / G0 X0 Y0 ; / S1200 M3 ; / G43 H10 Z120. ; / M8 ; / G65 P16xx ... ; / G0 Z100. ; / M9 ; / G53 H0 Z0 ; / M30 ; / %.",
  "Letter standard: X Y = center, W = start Z (face), Z = final Z, K = step down per turn, T = tool diameter, Q = stepover or radial increment, R = safety plane, F = feed.",
  "Macro alarm: IF [condition] THEN #3000 = n (TEXT) ; with its own range per macro (101-104 face milling, 111 bolt circle, 121-123 helix, 151-154 rectangular, 161-163 polygon, 171-176 radius, 211-216 keyway, 291-299 radius between diameters).",
  "An empty letter is not the same as 0: for Q use IF [#17 EQ 0] THEN #17 = #9 ; and IF [#17 EQ #0] THEN #17 = #9 ;.",
  "Calculations in #100 to #199; in a macro that calls another, use #27 to #33 (local) so they are not cleared.",
  "In a nested call, avoid the letters I, E, U and V (problem seen on the machine: I ended up in #7). In a new macro, use K or V for the thread pitch instead of I.",
  "Values with decimals in G65 always with a point (X215.). One decimal point per number.",
  "After G2/G3 always go back to G1 for the next linear moves.",
  "Do not rely on Block Delete (/): it locks up the Romi."]},
 {"t": "Simple parametric (no G65)", "items": [
  "# variables at the start, in order (#1, #2, #3...), only the ones needed: part size in #1, tool diameter in #2, path in #3.",
  "Tool number in its own variable, the last one in the list, used in T#n and G43 H#n.",
  "No .0 in variables and math (#1 = 100, [#1 - #2] / 2). Coordinates typed directly in the block keep the point (Z100.).",
  "A single variable for (hole diameter - cutter diameter) / 2, with brackets.",
  "Reset with a typed number (#5 = 0), with no extra variable.",
  "A single N and a single IF ... GOTO per loop. No WHILE/DO, FUP, THEN, turn counter or G65.",
  "Z increment directly in a variable. Never a fudge (+ 0.001) in the IF: pick an increment that comes out exact (0.5 / 0.25 / 0.125 / 0.0625).",
  "On profiles with several sides: #5 = #5 - #7 before each G1, with #7 = #6 / n. If the division is not exact (hexagon), compare the Z at the end of the turn and use another variable for the Z of each side.",
  "Bolt circle holes: angle limit always 360 (valid when the start angle is less than the increment; otherwise limit = start + 360).",
  "Roughing with round values; the exact value only in the one-pass finish.",
  "Comments in parentheses, short and without accents."]},
 {"t": "Approach and depth", "items": [
  "Start Z at the face (Z0) and going down, never starting from the bottom (also for threads).",
  "When a profile is done, go up to Z50. (not Z2).",
  "In XY, the G0 first goes 20 mm past the start point, on the same entry line (e.g. G0 X[#5 + 20] Y0), goes down in Z and enters with G1. In a hole or pocket, the offset point is the center."]},
 {"t": "Technical rules", "items": [
  "Outside profile climb milling: G2. Inside a hole or pocket: G3. Right-hand internal thread going down: G2 (conventional, preferred by the operator).",
  "Bolt circle: X = R * COS[angle], Y = R * SIN[angle]; G52 moves the origin to the hole center and does not add up.",
  "Hexagon: across corners = across flats / COS[30]. d = across flats / 2 + cutter radius; corner R = d / SIN[60]; half corner R * COS[60].",
  "FANUC alarms if the start and end radius of a G2/G3 are different: radii and chamfers are done in steps (G1 to the point + full flat circle).",
  "30° chamfer measured horizontally: Δradius = Δz / TAN[30].",
  "Radius with a square-corner cutter: offset = SIN[angle] * R and Z = [COS[angle] - 1] * R.",
  "On threads and radii around a hole, F is at the cutter center; at the cutting edge the feed is much higher.",
  "G68 is a control option (cancel with G69). PS0127 = block with NC command and macro mixed."]},
 {"t": "File and transfer", "items": [
  "Plain text (.txt or .nc) with % on the first and last line, ; at the end of each block, no blank lines and no accents.",
  "Name with the O number (e.g. O0033.txt). The number must not already exist in the machine.",
  "FAT32 USB stick in the panel USB port. In EDIT: PROG, (OPRT), READ, number and EXEC.",
  "First part in Single Block with reduced feed; first check in Machine Lock or without material."]},
]
